I'd like to use, and put somewhere publically, a bash script that simply
uses CVS and wget to fetch the right components and builds a 2.4
(maybe 2.5 if wanted) ALSA enabled kernel. Sure, it's probably simple
enough to put together but I suspect a number of people already have
done so. If anyone cares to send anything to mailto:markc@renta.net
I'll hang any working results at alsa.opensrc.org, with attributes.

I'd like to extend it to including ardour and other apps eventually but
right now I (and lots of other novices?) just need a working kernel !
(I have Athlon and Duron machines and both lock up hard with ALSA)

